    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "The fix is complete! I've updated `src/money.js` to use `Math.round()` when converting decimal prices to whole cents. This eliminates the floating-point precision errors that were causing `39.95 * 100` to become `3995.0000000000005`.\n\n**What was changed:**\n- Line 13 in `parseEuros()`: Changed `Number(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')).toFixed(2)) * 100` to `Math.round(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')) * 100)`\n- Line 25 in `cellCents()`: Changed `Number(s) * 100` to `Math.round(Number(s) * 100)`\n\n**Verification:**\n- All 50 tests pass \u2713\n- Your 39.95 gym membership now correctly parses as `3995` cents (whole number) \u2713\n- Netflix (12.99 \u2192 1299) and Spotify (10.99 \u2192 1099) continue to work \u2713\n\nThe changes are staged and ready to commit.",
